  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA) yielding ~48.5% accuracy. We have zero information about whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task. The most critical unknown is whether image features are informative at all, since this determines whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing. 2) What this tests: config_010 (image-only, single-profile, ResNet-50) establishes a second modality anchor under the same single-profile setting as config_001, isolating the effect of modality (RNA vs. image) while keeping profile complexity constant. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: Before investing budget in the large multimodal design space (configs 016–051), we must know whether each modality individually contributes. If image-only performs comparably to or worse than RNA-only, multimodal fusion is unlikely to add much and we should focus on improving the RNA encoder or profile setting. If image-only is substantially stronger, multimodal fusion becomes a high-priority direction. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design axis (modality) under the limited budget."
}

